<title>USA: Puget Power storm losses could top $10 mln.</title>
<headline>Puget Power storm losses could top $10 mln.</headline>
<dateline>LOS ANGELES 1997-01-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Puget Sound Power and Light Co's losses from recent Pacific Northwest storms will probably top $10 million, the company said Friday.</p>
<p>But Puget Power spokeswoman Betty Werblun emphasized a final tally of storm damage has not been completed.</p>
<p>&quot;We are still working the storm. Our goal is to have power restored to everybody by midnight,&quot; she said.</p>
<p>As of early Friday, over 2,000 of Puget Power's customers had no power, compared with a peak of more than 250,000 in the first stages of the storm series which began more than a week ago.</p>
<p>--D Beasley, Los Angeles bureau + 1 213 955 6761</p>
